  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">Introduction</h3>
      <p>Social security and Medicare taxes are collected by the Internal Revenue Service (IRS). These taxes are paid by the employees and the employer each pay half of the taxes. Under the Federal Insurance Contributions Act (FICA), the employer and the employee each pay half of the taxes. No earnings subject to these taxes are exempt.</p>
      <p>This publication covers the following topics about the collection of social security and Medicare taxes from members of the clergy and religious workers.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><span data-field="introduction_point_1">{{ introduction_point_1 }}</span></li>
        <li><span data-field="introduction_point_2">{{ introduction_point_2 }}</span></li>
        <li><span data-field="introduction_point_3">{{ introduction_point_3 }}</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p>This publication also covers certain income tax rules of interest to the clergy. A comprehensive example shows filled-in worksheets for a minister who has not taken a vow of poverty. This publication also covers the tax reporting of items specific to the clergy.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">Table 1. Are You Covered Under FICA or SECA?</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th style="width: 30%;">Occupation</th>
            <th style="width: 35%;">Covered Under FICA?</th>
            <th style="width: 35%;">Covered Under SECA?</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Minister</td>
            <td>NO. You are exempt.*</td>
            <td>YES, if you do not have an approved exemption from the self-employment tax.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Member of a religious order who has not taken a vow of poverty</td>
            <td>NO. You are exempt.*</td>
            <td>NO, if you have an approved exemption from the self-employment tax.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Member of a religious order who has taken a vow of poverty</td>
            <td>YES, if you are an employee of the church.</td>
            <td>NO. You are exempt.*</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Other</td>
            <td>NO, if neither of the above applies.</td>
            <td>YES, if you do not have an approved exemption.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p style="font-size: 0.85em;">* The exemption applies only to qualified services, as defined later under Qualified Services.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

