  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">Social Security Coverage</h3>
      <p>The services you perform in the exercise of your religious duties may be covered by social security and Medicare taxes. Your earnings for these services are subject to social security and Medicare taxes unless one of the following applies:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><span data-field="coverage_point_1">{{ coverage_point_1 }}</span></li>
        <li><span data-field="coverage_point_2">{{ coverage_point_2 }}</span></li>
        <li><span data-field="coverage_point_3">{{ coverage_point_3 }}</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p>For more information, see <span data-field="reference_ss_tax">{{ reference_ss_tax }}</span>.</p>
      <p><strong>Ministers</strong></p>
      <p>Ministers are individuals who are duly ordained, commissioned, or licensed by a religious body to perform religious duties. They are given the authority to conduct religious worship, perform sacramental functions, and administer religious rites.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">Qualified Services</h3>
      <p>Qualified services are services performed in the exercise of your religious duties. If you are a minister or religious worker, your services are considered qualified services if they are performed in the exercise of your religious duties.</p>
      <p>The following discussions provide more detailed information on qualified services for ministers and religious workers.</p>
      <p><strong>Ministers</strong></p>
      <p>Ministers perform services such as preaching, teaching, counseling, and administering religious rites. These services are considered qualified services.</p>
      <p><strong>Religious workers</strong></p>
      <p>Religious workers perform services such as counseling, teaching, and administering religious rites. These services are considered qualified services.</p>
      <p><strong>Other services</strong></p>
      <p>Services that are not performed in the exercise of religious duties are not considered qualified services. Examples include administrative tasks, teaching outside of religious duties, and performing services for non-religious organizations.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
