  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">Exemption From Self-Employment (SE) Tax</h3>
      <p>You can request an exemption from SE tax if you meet one of the following requirements:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><span data-field="se_tax_req_1">{{ se_tax_req_1 }}</span></li>
        <li><span data-field="se_tax_req_2">{{ se_tax_req_2 }}</span></li>
        <li><span data-field="se_tax_req_3">{{ se_tax_req_3 }}</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p>To claim the exemption from SE tax, you must file Form 4361 or Form 4362.</p>
      <p><strong>Form 4361</strong></p>
      <p>This form is for ministers and religious workers who are not members of a religious order.</p>
      <p><strong>Form 4362</strong></p>
      <p>This form is for members of a religious order.</p>
      <p><strong>When to file.</strong></p>
      <p>You must file the exemption form with your tax return for the year you want the exemption to apply.</p>
      <p><strong>Approval.</strong></p>
      <p>If approved, you will receive an approval letter from the IRS.</p>
      <p><strong>Effective Date.</strong></p>
      <p>For all tax years after 1967 in which you have at least $400 of net earnings from self-employment.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">Members of Religious Orders</h3>
      <p>If you are a member of a religious order who has not taken a vow of poverty, you may be subject to self-employment tax. You may apply for an exemption from payment of self-employment tax if you meet certain requirements.</p>
      <p><strong>Services covered under FICA at the election of the order.</strong> If you are a member of a religious order, you may be able to elect to have your services covered under FICA. If you make this election, the religious order will pay the taxes.</p>
      <p><strong>Tax filing.</strong></p>
      <p>If you are covered under FICA, you are not subject to self-employment tax. You will report your earnings on your tax return, but you will not pay self-employment tax.</p>
      <p><strong>Who can apply.</strong></p>
      <p>Members of religious orders who meet the requirements for an exemption may apply using Form 4029.</p>
      <p><strong>File online.</strong></p>
      <p>You can file Form 4029 online through the IRS website.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
