  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">Ministers Defined</h3>
      <p>Ministers are individuals who are duly ordained, commissioned, or licensed by a religious body to perform religious duties. They are given the authority to conduct religious worship, perform sacramental functions, and administer religious rites.</p>
      <p><strong>Ministers performing sacrificial functions.</strong></p>
      <p>Ministers who perform sacrificial functions are considered to be performing religious duties.</p>
      <p><strong>Ministers performing non-sacrificial functions.</strong></p>
      <p>Ministers who perform non-sacrificial functions are considered to be performing religious duties.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">Church or Associated Institution</h3>
      <p>A church or an associated institution, you are considered to be an agent of the religious body that employs you.</p>
      <p><strong>Employer responsibilities.</strong></p>
      <p>The employer is responsible for withholding and paying the taxes for the clergy.</p>
      <p><strong>Employee responsibilities.</strong></p>
      <p>The clergy is responsible for reporting their earnings and paying any taxes that are not withheld.</p>
      <p><strong>Tax liability.</strong></p>
      <p>The tax liability depends on the employment status of the clergy.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <span>Page 7 of 27 of Publication 517</span>
