  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <div class="section-title">Foreign Earned Income</div>
      <p>Certain income may be exempt from income tax if you work in a foreign country or in a specified foreign place. You may also claim an exclusion for foreign earned income. Publication 570. Tax Guide for Individuals with Income from Foreign Sources. For more information, see Publication 570. Tax Guide for Individuals with Income from Foreign Sources. For more information, see IRS.gov or contact your local IRS office.</p>
      <div class="section-title">Expense Items</div>
      <p>The tax treatment of ministerial trade or business expenses, expenses allowable to tax-free income, and health insurance costs is discussed in Publication 570.</p>
      <div class="section-title">Ministerial Trade or Business Expenses</div>
      <p>When you figure your income tax, you must determine your deductions on Schedule A (Form 1040). You may deduct certain trade or business expenses incurred while working as an employee. You may also have to deduct expenses incurred while working as an independent contractor. For more information, see Publication 570.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <div class="section-title">Example.</div>
