    <li style="font-size: 10pt;">You had self-employment income from other than church employee income (line 4 of Short Schedule SE or line 4c of Long Schedule SE) of $400 or more.</li>
    <li style="font-size: 10pt;">You had church employee income of $108.28 or more. Income from services you performed as a minister or a member of a religious order, church, or religious sect is not subject to self-employment tax.</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Note. Even if you had a loss or amount of income from self-employment, it may be to your benefit to file Schedule SE and use either "optional method" in Part II of Long Schedule SE (see page SE-3). Exception. If you had $4361 and received IRS approval not to be taxed on these earnings, do not file Schedule SE. Instead, write "Exempt-Form 4361" on Form 1040, line 58.</p>

